<title>FRANCE: French industry optimistic on output -Feb survey.</title>
<headline>French industry optimistic on output -Feb survey.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted data in its February survey of industrialists' views.</p>
<p>A positive figure shows the percentage points by which the percentage of respondents saying things had improved or risen outnumbered the percentage saying things had worsened.</p>
<p>					Feb   Jan  Dec  Nov  Oct  Sep  Jul</p>
<p> Recent past output		-5    -7    3   -2   -8    1   -9</p>
<p> Finished product stocks	 20    20   17   18   16   20   27</p>
<p> Overall orders and demand    -23   -28  -28  -25  -25  -25  -35</p>
<p> Foreign orders and demand     -1    -4   -3   -4  -16  -18  -25</p>
<p> Future output (overall)	  6     1  -14  -21  -23  -29  -28</p>
<p> Future output (personal)	 6     4    4    3    3    5    3</p>
<p> Future prices (overall)	-10   -13  -21  -25  -31  -26  -22</p>
<p> Future prices (personal)	-3   -22  -19  -15  -11  -14   -9</p>
<p>Recent past output (breakdown)</p>
<p> Agri-food businesses	    16    12   25    8    9    8 -11</p>
<p> Energy			     -89   -86   -4   -7  -75   22 -11</p>
<p> Manufacturing output	     2    -2    3   -2   -3   -1  -8</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods	     -2   -10   -5   -3  -15   -8 -15</p>
<p> Industrial capital goods	 4    14   11   -3    2   -6   0</p>
<p> Cars and land transport	-33   -37  -47  -44   20   39 -23</p>
<p> Consumer goods		     1     0   16   10   -2    8   6</p>
<p>Future output, personal (breakdown)</p>
<p> Agri-food businesses	     2   -12   10    8    7   -4 -26</p>
<p> Energy			     -86   -86    2   -7   61   -3  12</p>
<p> Manufacturing output	    10    11    5    4    1    5   3</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods	     11    11    0    5    6   -3  -2</p>
<p> Industrial capital goods	10     9   15    3    6    8   7</p>
<p> Cars and land transport	 21    19   -8  -29  -30   22   7</p>
<p> Consumer goods		     5     4   -4   10   -2    4  -3</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +(33-1) 42 21 54 52</p>
